port-edits/ -- our changes to the pret decompilation and the Nitro SDKs, as edit scripts that carry only our own text.

tools/sync_port.sh copies the pristine pret tree into port/ and then runs tools/apply_edits.py, which applies every
port-edits/<pret path>.ed to port/<pret path> and copies every file under port-edits/new/ to port/<same path>. These
replaced the unified diffs of port-patches/ (2026-10-15, release slice P1): a diff repeats the original lines as context
and removed lines, an .ed file never does.

THE .ed FORMAT
One .ed per pret file (so one owner per file). It starts with a header:

    3DP-edit 1
    path <pret path>                    must match the .ed's own location under port-edits/
    sha1 <SHA-1 of the pristine file>   at the pinned pret commit; any other content is refused
    pret c248fb3f8cc9934ded800e489567c5c0eeee92eb
    final-newline yes|no                only when the result's final newline differs from the pristine file's

then operations, each on ORIGINAL line numbers (1-based), so they never depend on each other:

    @N delete K           remove original lines N .. N+K-1
    @N insert-before K    followed by K payload lines, inserted before original line N
    @N insert-after K     followed by K payload lines, inserted after original line N (used for the end of the file)
    @N splice C L         followed by 1 payload line: it replaces bytes [C, C+L) of original line N (C counts from 0)

A payload line is '|' and then our text, up to the newline. A splice carries only the new bytes, never the text around
them, so a near-copy of an original line (a renamed field, a changed constant) costs a few bytes.

Order: the result equals applying the ops bottom-up by line and right-to-left by column. Between two original lines,
the insert-after ops of the upper line come first, then the insert-before ops of the lower line; ops at the same
position keep their written order. The applier refuses, and writes nothing at all, on: a malformed file, a SHA-1
mismatch, a CR byte (clone with core.autocrlf=false), two deletes sharing a line, a splice on a deleted line, two
splices on one line whose byte ranges overlap or start at the same column, an op past the end of the file or line, or a
new/ file that would overwrite a different existing file.

CHANGING AN EDIT
1. Edit the file in port/ (after tools/sync_port.sh).
2. python3 -I tools/mkedit.py --write <pret path> [...]   regenerates port-edits/<pret path>.ed from the pristine file
   ($PLAT_REF: your pret checkout, see BUILDING.md) and port/<pret path>; a file pret does not have goes to new/, and an
   .ed whose file is back to pristine is removed. mkedit applies its output back and refuses unless it reproduces the
   port/ file byte for byte. (python3 -I tools/mkedit.py PRISTINE EDITED > x.ed prints one .ed.)
3. tools/sync_port.sh again: it must reproduce your port/ file.
4. make check-edit-text: no run of 40+ characters of the carried text may appear in the pristine pret tree, except
   the lines listed in tools/check_edit_text_allow.txt (prototype and identifier lines); see that tool's header.
5. make host-tests: tools/host-tests/port_edits_test.py regenerates every .ed and must get the committed bytes back.

OWNERSHIP
Rule 5 of the private design notes treats this file as the authority on which edit set owns a pret file. The
sets keep the names of the patches they came from; the list of files per set is at the end.

game-gcc-fixes               slice 1.2c. 53 game/lib files: the mwcc-isms GCC 15 rejects (static after non-static, cast-as-lvalue, const-member
                             struct assignment, VLA initializer, implicit int / function / pointer conversions, missing prototypes, a header-guard
                             collision). Per-class table: the private design notes ("slice 1.2c").
nitrosdk-asm-to-c            slice 1.2b. The mwcc `asm` function bodies of the NitroSDK ARM9 census set (30 files) become C, or
                             stubs over the HWOS_* hooks of port-shim/include/hw_os_hooks.h; the originals stay under
                             `#if defined(__MWERKS__) || defined(SDK_CW)`. Adds lib/crypto/src/rc4_encrypt.c (C RC4 Encrypt and
                             FastEncrypt for asm/rc4.s and rc4_fast.s). Per-function table: the private design notes.
nitrosdk-memmap              bet 1.3. The DS memory map redirected to host arrays: the base macros of hw/ARM9/mmap_global.h (and HW_MAIN_MEM_SHARED in
                             mmap_main.h) become `(u32)g_hw*` under SDK_GCC; common/mmap_shared.h's 56 `HW_MAIN_MEM + 0x007ffNNN` fields become
                             `HW_MAIN_MEM_SHARED + 0xNNN`; gx_load3d.c's texture tables store slot offset + 1 (a shifted address is not a constant).
                             the private design notes.
nitrosdk-gcc-branches        slice 1.2a + 1.2c. The SDK's SDK_GCC branches (16 TO BE DEFINED headers, nitro/types.h); 1.2c adds the
                             aligned(4) on s64/u64 (ABI parity with mwcc).
nitrosdk-gcc-fixes           slice 1.2c. 9 SDK / NitroSystem / NitroWiFi files: static-after-non-static, cast-as-lvalue, implicit int, __alloca,
                             u64 for the two raw `unsigned long long` struct members.

Review 1.2 fixes (2026-10-12) touched these edit sets: MWCC_BITFIELD_UNIT_END in nitro/types.h (nitrosdk-gcc-branches) and its uses
(battle_mon.h, list_menu.h, naming_screen.c, struct_ov17_022444BC.h in game-gcc-fixes; snd/common/work.h in nitrosdk-gcc-fixes);
`static inline` for mul64 and the other plain `inline` helpers; `return` in ov61_0222DD30.

Bet 1.3 also touched nitrosdk-asm-to-c: os_exception.c (HW_EXCP_VECTOR_BUF_FOR_DEBUGGER follows the redirected system page) and
os_system.c (OS_SpinWait calls HWOS_SpinWait, a yield point).

Review 1.3 fixes (2026-10-12):
nitrosdk-devices             bet 1.3. The device hooks (port-shim/include/hw_dev_hooks.h): timer.h (control write -> HWOS_TimerControlWrite),
                             pxi_fifo.c (PXI_InitFifo takes its EMULATOR branch under SDK_GCC: OS_IsRunOnEmulator() is FALSE in a final-ROM
                             build and the ARM7 INTF handshake would never end; FIFO regs go through the loopback), mi_dma.c (CNT write ->
                             HWDEV_DmaStart; MIi_CheckDma0SourceAddress a no-op under SDK_GCC), cp/divider.h and cp/sqrt.h (operand/control
                             write -> HWDEV_CpDivRun / HWDEV_CpSqrtRun). the private design notes.
Also added to the older sets: nitrosdk-asm-to-c (31 files; cp_context.c calls the CP hooks), nitrosdk-memmap (7 files; HW_SND_PTR_MIN,
HW_MAIN_MEM_SHARED_END / SYSTEM_END, SNDi_PTR_MIN in snd_bank.c / snd_command.c), nitrosdk-gcc-fixes (15 files; DWC gsAssert.h
__msl_assertion_failed prototype and the nonport.c build fixes).

nitrosdk-vramcnt             bet 2.1b. Every VRAMCNT_A..I store becomes HWVRAM_STORE(BANK, v) (ioreg_GX.h macro: the register byte, then HWVRAM_SetCnt of
                             port-shim/include/hw_dev_hooks.h): gx_vramcnt.c (135 sites), gxstate.c (GX_InitGXState resets all nine banks). The bulk
                             writers MIi_Cpu* / MI_CpuFill8 / MI_CpuCopy8 call HWVRAM_Touch (dirty pages) inside nitrosdk-asm-to-c (mi_memory.c is owned
                             there). mi_wram.c writes WRAMCNT (0x247), not a bank: untouched. the private design notes.

Bet 2.1e review fix P-S1 (2026-10-13): the sets below were missing from this list; each entry names its files.

nitrosdk-card-fs             bet 1.4. card/src/card_rom.c (the three card registers CARDCNT / data go through HWDEV_CardCtrlRead / Write / DataRead under SDK_GCC: they have
                             side effects, a read streams the page; no DMA-timed card path) and fs/src/fs_overlay.c (FS_LoadOverlayImage[Async], FS_StartOverlay, FS_EndOverlay
                             call HWDEV_Overlay{Load,Start,Unload}). the private design notes.
nitrosdk-snd-arm7            bet 1.5. snd/src/snd_main.c, snd/src/snd_util.c and include/nitro/hw/ARM7/mmap_global.h: the ARM7 sound driver compiled with SDK_ARM7 + SDK_GCC runs on
                             the ARM11 next to the ARM9 code (its register accesses go to the host I/O block, HW_SND_PTR_MIN, the DS-BIOS table lookups are compiled out, the
                             SND thread entry points are compiled out). the private design notes.
